  lib_runtime.pcpp - Build-kind compliance: a lib that uses the runtime

  This lib's code calls into the PaskalCPP runtime (div: checked, raises on a
  zero divisor), so it gets a startup hook and pcpp builds pcpp_runtime and
  publishes it beside the lib. A PaskalCPP program that links the lib brings
  its own runtime and never links pcpp_runtime (lib_runtime_host.pcpp: a raise
  inside the lib is caught by the program's guard); a C program built by
  another toolchain links the lib, then pcpp_runtime, through a C++ driver
  (lib_runtime_host.c). lib_plain.pcpp is the other case.
  It builds and is not run: lib_runtime_host.pcpp holds the output to expect.

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\lib_runtime.pcpp
    pcpp res\tests\lib_runtime.pcpp -t x86_64-linux-gnu
  CHECK: each prints "Publishing pcpp_runtime.lib to ..." (Linux: libpcpp_runtime.a);
  output\lib holds lib_runtime.lib and pcpp_runtime.lib (windows),
  liblib_runtime.a and libpcpp_runtime.a (linux).
  Then lib_runtime_host.pcpp (a PaskalCPP program that links it).

  A C program built by another toolchain: the lib, then pcpp_runtime, a C++ driver:
    res\zig\zig.exe c++ -target x86_64-windows-gnu res\tests\lib_runtime_host.c output\lib\lib_runtime.lib output\lib\pcpp_runtime.lib -o output\lib_runtime_c.exe
    output\lib_runtime_c.exe
    res\zig\zig.exe c++ -target x86_64-linux-gnu res\tests\lib_runtime_host.c output\lib\liblib_runtime.a output\lib\libpcpp_runtime.a -o output\lib_runtime_c
    wsl ./output/lib_runtime_c
  CHECK: both print   from C: lib_rt_div(7, 2) = 3
  and the [Heap] line (pcpp_runtime was built debug, as the lib), exit code 0.

  Break it (by hand):
    1. do the C program steps (windows) with "cc" for "c++" and without the
       pcpp_runtime.lib argument.
       CHECK: lld-link: error: undefined symbol: pcpp::init(int, char**)
       (and pcpp::enter, pcpp::raise, libc++ names: the lib calls the runtime)
*******************************************************************************/

module lib lib_runtime;

exported routine clink lib_rt_div(AA: int32; AB: int32): int32;
begin
  return AA div AB;
end;

end.
